  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I recently tried the Android port on my phone and was dismayed that the only microphone option is push-to-talk-AND-mute-everyone-else.  VR Chat is a very social platform, and not being able to speak and listen at the same time makes communicating rather difficult.  If someone starts talking over me, I'm only aware if I'm looking at them and can see their mouth animating.  I keep missing parts of conversations.\n\nGiven that this is on my *phone*, a device specifically designed for holding two way conversations even over speakerphone, it seems odd that it's one-way for VRC.  Especially as I could plug in headphones and definitely not have sound leaking.  (I don't know if there's a hidden settings option when using headphones - I don't have headphoens with me to check but the settings UI makes me think that's not an option)\n\nI assume that this is to avoid feedback, but it's a bit too harsh a limitation.  It makes the phone app very limited in utility.  It's a pity, as otherwise it's a wonderful way to keep in touch with friends while traveling.",
